{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Complete direct 3-CNF reduction for the source’s aggregate all-root undirected spanning-tree objective. The explicitly encoded nonnegative-integer decision version is strongly NP-complete, with costs only 0, 1 and n+1. Includes unchanged proof and separate adversarial AI review: 78,056 author checks and 600,122 independent Prüfer-tree/edge-cut checks, with NP membership, both reduction directions and noncanonical trees covered. Actual approach count is 2/5. The adjacent fixed-root directed path-cost problem has a related independently developed literal-selection mechanism; no equivalence or two unrelated discoveries are claimed. Novelty and human peer review are unestablished. Parent coordinates claimed_solved queue status.","headRefName":"dot/math-30003996","headRefOid":"3526d46bf143b08e5055ffa7728c6278e9f958ea","isDraft":true,"number":108,"state":"OPEN","title":"All-root spanning trees: independently reviewed strong NP-completeness","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/108"}
